    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Done Kirgnien\nDONG KINGMAN\nMIAMI",
      "Cocktaiko\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum Premium Beer\nMenus\nApéritif\nI NO 174\nSelected Gourmet Delicacies\n#8****\nRoast au Vol\nA selected cut of aged beef\nroasted on board and carved to order\n*5*0-2F E-\u003e\nSeafood Platter\nCold Lush Seafood with a Tangy Japanese Sauce\nBreast of Chicken Oriental\n** #L8\nTrout Grenobloise\nTrout Sauteed with Capers, Lemon, Butter and Fresh Parsley\n4a0 12202\nPlat du Jour",
      "Trout Grenobloise\nTrout Sauteed with Capers, Lemon, Butter and Fresh Parsley\nPlat du Jour\nSteamed Rice\n→ 1\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nPotatoes Maison\nCoffee\n3-E-\nTossed Garden Salad\n1 5 5\n#*\"#\nSelection of Cheeses and Fruits\n*t**x2+\nDessert\n+Y-r\nTea\nGreen Tea\n*\n*I*\nDecaffeinated Coffee\n**\nT. 370) Ma\nSelected French Wines\nFrench Champagne Brut\nDrambuie Amaretto di Saronno Bénédictine\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP\nContreau\n236 KJC",
      "MIAMI\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting the beautiful,\nthe monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than fortv\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nHere he depicts Miami, city of glitter and glamour, of sun and sand, of gleaming highrise hotels and condominiums.\nHost to millions who come for the pleasure of basking amid palms and flowers in this the hub of tropical South Florida\nOne of the most renowned playgrounds in the world, Miami offers a variety of recreation. From golf and tennis to\ndeepsea fishing and yachting. From thoroughbred racing to the \"Son et Lumière\" presentations at exquisite Vizcaya\nMiami also serves as gateway to the Caribbean Cruise World. From here luxury liners offer frequent sailings in\nconjunction with Pan Am's \"Air-Sea\" Flights,\nPan Am jets land at Miami's busy International Airport from all major cities on its US network, from Central and\nSouth America and key European cities such as London, Paris and Frankfurt.\nPAN AM.\n2007.054.016"
    ],
